    "file": "arrow/cpp/src/arrow/array/array_dict.cc",
    "description": "The crash is an assertion-abort triggered by constructing a DictionaryArray from malformed ArrayData where `data->dictionary == nullptr`. In `DictionaryArray::DictionaryArray(const std::shared_ptr<ArrayData>&)`, `ARROW_CHECK_NE(data->dictionary, nullptr)` fires and logs FATAL, causing `abort()` in `arrow/util/logging.cc` (CerrLog destructor). The bad ArrayData is produced while reading a dictionary delta and recursively materializing nested list/dictionary values (`DictionaryMemo::AddDictionaryDelta` -> `MakeArray(dictionary)`), so untrusted IPC dictionary metadata can reach DictionaryArray construction without prior rejection.",
    "conditions": "In `arrow-ipc-stream-fuzz`, attacker-controlled IPC stream bytes are parsed by `ReadDictionary` in `arrow/cpp/src/arrow/ipc/reader.cc`. A crafted DictionaryBatch with `isDelta=true` and nested types (list containing dictionary-typed child) is loaded into ArrayData such that a dictionary-typed node lacks its backing `dictionary` pointer. During `DictionaryMemo::AddDictionaryDelta` (`arrow/cpp/src/arrow/ipc/dictionary.cc`), `MakeArray(dictionary)` recursively instantiates arrays (`ListArray` -> child `MakeArray` -> `DictionaryArray`), hitting `ARROW_CHECK_NE(data->dictionary, nullptr)` and aborting. This is a reachable DoS via malformed IPC input."
